{"id": "99d34a5e-c53f-468e-991c-7df0d1cbba10", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T14:27:44.415009", "source": "user", "parent_id": "6201d75f-373b-401a-81cd-372075242f0e", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"This is a design-only assignment; no experiment execution is expected. For this initial inspection, I would like you to (1) inspect the workspace at /workspace to see whether any QuaRot source files, LLaMa-2 config shards, evaluation scripts, or pre-existing notes are already present (use `ls`, targeted `find`, and `head`/`grep`; the bubblewrap runtime has no network and dependencies are not preinstalled, so treat any externally required packages as unavailable). (2) State the proposed experimental design approach for answering: 'How does QuaRot's end-to-end 4-bit quantization affect the prefill and decoding performance of LLaMa-2 models?'. The proposal should cover the model variants (e.g., LLaMa-2 7B vs 13B, and optionally 70B if compute permits), the precision/quantization conditions (FP16 baseline vs QuaRot end-to-end W4A4, and usefully an intermediate such as weight-only W4A16 as a reference), the workload definitions that cleanly separate prefill from decoding (e.g., controlled prompt lengths for prefill TTFT, controlled generation length with fixed context for decoding TPOT/throughput, and a long-context sweep so prefill cost is non-trivial), the datasets/inputs (e.g., WikiText-2 or C4 prompts, plus a perplexity and a generative-quality probe such as MMLU or a small LM-Eval-Harness subset), the measurement protocol (batch sizes, warm-up, number of runs, median vs mean, hardware counters of interest: latency, throughput tokens/s, peak memory), and the analysis plan (paired comparisons, effect sizes, breakdown of prefill vs decoding, sensitivity to sequence length). (3) List the consequential assumptions and uncertainties, including: hardware assumptions (single GPU class), lack of real GPU in this environment, reliance on the published QuaRot methodology and LLaMa-2 weight access policies, choice of KV-cache quantization interactions, expected direction and magnitude of effect (you may hypothesize, label it as such, not measure it), and what would constitute a meaningful prefill vs decoding impact threshold. Do not produce the final design yet; awaiting approach review before approval.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How does QuaRot's end-to-end 4-bit quantization affect the prefill and decoding performance of LLaMa-2 models?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
