{"id": "8e3ef13a-59d5-4667-ade4-c3833ff02b16", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T14:27:54.258122", "source": "environment", "parent_id": "0a3d6cad-6f9c-4ff7-b8d1-435a5b2d80ee", "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "call-e6dc5a68-cdba-4517-b1a3-b60ddb837c63", "observation": {"content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"phase\": \"exploration\", \"command\": \"uname -a && nproc && free -h 2>/dev/null && which nvidia-smi 2>&1\", \"exit_code\": 127, \"timed_out\": false, \"elapsed_seconds\": 0.016, \"output\": \"Linux d33eaef-lcedt 7.0.0-38-generic #38~24.04.4-Ubuntu SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Mon Sep 14 16:37:11 UTC 2 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux\\n24\\n               total        used        free      shared  buff/cache   available\\nMem:           125Gi        20Gi        52Gi       130Mi        52Gi       104Gi\\nSwap:           61Gi       3.7Gi        58Gi\\n/bin/bash: line 1: which: command not found\\n\", \"output_truncated\": false}"}], "is_error": false, "kind": "BenchmarkObservation"}, "action_id": "92a5e2db-fedc-4e1a-9f36-0a5ef1cc500e", "extended_content": [], "kind": "ObservationEvent", "source_event_index": 15}
{"id": "8cb37a67-ef0c-4c2b-83ab-b02ecfa101cc", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T14:28:50.307689", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "8e3ef13a-59d5-4667-ade4-c3833ff02b16", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-3769a13b-2a98-45a0-b9f4-424b71ec48f2", "tool_call": {"id": "call-3769a13b-2a98-45a0-b9f4-424b71ec48f2", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Propose experimental-design approach for QuaRot on LLaMa-2\",\"stage\":\"plan\",\"answer\":\"## Repository observations\\n\\n- `/workspace` contains only `task.json`. No `quarot/`, no LLaMa-2 shards/json, no evaluation scripts, no notes.\\n- Python 3.12.3 present, system Python. No project deps installed, `which` not on PATH, `nvidia-smi` absent.\\n- 24 CPU threads, ~125 GiB RAM, no GPU detected. Network is disabled.\\n- Implication: any concrete execution of the design must happen in a different environment than this one; this environment can only produce the experiment plan.\\n\\n## Proposed experimental-design approach\\n\\n### 1. Model variants\\n- Primary: **LLaMa-2 7B** and **LLaMa-2 13B**. Both fit and are reproducible end-to-end on a single high-end GPU.\\n- Optional extension: **LLaMa-2 70B**, only if multi-GPU or 80GB-class memory + CPU offload is granted; otherwise described as out of scope to avoid pretending a measurement we cannot honor.\\n- Hold the Meta-released revision constant (no fine-tunes) so the FP16 vs W4A4 comparison is purely the quantization effect and not a checkpoint effect.\\n\\n### 2. Precision / quantization conditions (paired within model)\\nPer model, three conditions (same calibration data, same generation code-path):\\n- **FP16 baseline** — unrotated FP16 weights, FP16 activations, FP16 KV-cache. Control.\\n- **W4A16 reference** — weight-only 4-bit (RTN or GPTQ, matching what QuaRot uses pre-rotation), FP16 activations. Intermediate, isolates the weight-quant contribution.\\n- **QuaRot end-to-end W4A4** — Hadamard-rotated weights and activations quantized to 4-bit, with the paper's learned per-channel / per-head clipping and outlier handling; KV-cache left in FP16 (QuaRot default unless the researcher wants to add the +KV4 variant as a fourth cell).\\n\\n### 3. Workload definitions (prefill cleanly separated from decoding)\\n- **Prefill-only (TTFT).** Prompt lengths: {256, 512, 1024, 2048, 4096, 8192} tokens, `max_new_tokens=1` so decoding contributes negligibly. Metric: TTFT wall-clock per request, captured via a `cuda.Event` around the prefill phase.\\n- **Decode-only (TPOT and tokens/s).** Fixed prefill context (e.g. 512 tokens), generation lengths {64, 256, 512}. Metric: per-token decode latency (TPOT = (end-to-end − TTFT) / N), aggregate tokens/s.\\n- **Long-context sweep.** Same prefill cells as above, extending into 8k+ to make activation-bandwidth differences visible; remaining within LLaMa-2's 4k trained window by truncation, or using RoPE extension that QuaRot does not modify.\\n- **Mixed (realistic serving) workload.** Cartesian product of a smaller set of {prompt_len × gen_len} so total latency and aggregate tokens/s can be reported jointly.\\n\\n### 4. Datasets / inputs\\n- **Prefill prompts:** WikiText-2 raw test split (natural language, no contamination from train/calibration); a held-out C4 sample as a secondary diversity check.\\n- **Calibration:** WikiText-2 train, several hundred sequences of fixed length — strictly for rotation and clipping search, never used for evaluation. This mirrors the QuaRot paper's default and keeps quality probes clean.\\n- **Quality probes (guardrails, not the core performance question):**\\n  - WikiText-2 test perplexity.\\n  - A small LM-Eval-Harness subset: HellaSwag, ARC-Easy, PIQA, WinoGrande (zero-shot), to bound accuracy drift under W4A4.\\n\\n### 5. Measurement protocol\\n- **Batch sizes:** {1, 4, 8, optionally 16 if VRAM allows} — exposes both interactive and small-batch-throughput regimes.\\n- **Warmup:** 3–5 untimed calls per cell to amortize kernel/JIT compile and allocator state.\\n- **Timed runs:** ≥30 measurements per (model × condition × batch × length) cell; report median and p95 plus IQR.\\n- **Counters of interest:** TTFT (ms), TPOT (ms/token), aggregate tokens/s, peak GPU memory (allocated and reserved via `torch.cuda`), decode-only wall-time. Optional kernel-level timings via `torch.profiler` for one representative cell.\\n- **Determinism:** fixed prompt IDs across conditions; fixed seeds for any sampling; identical tokenization; identical kernel stack across conditions; the same generated length per cell.\\n\\n### 6. Analysis plan\\n- **Paired comparisons.** For each request id, compute Δ = T_quant − T_fp16 and analyze the paired distribution (Wilcoxon signed-rank, paired t-test, sign test as a robustness check).\\n- **Effect size.** Report relative slowdown = T_quant / T_fp16 − 1, plus Cohen's d on log-latency.\\n- **Decomposition.** Tabulate prefill (TTFT) and decode (TPOT, tokens/s) effects independently before any end-to-end number, so the phases are not conflated.\\n- **Sensitivity.** TTFT vs prompt length; TPOT vs context length and vs batch size; quality Δ vs condition.\\n- **Cross-model.** 7B vs 13B (and 70B if available) — does the relative benefit of W4A4 scale with model size / memory pressure?\\n- **Quality guardrail.** Δ perplexity and Δ accuracy on the LM-Eval subset, reported with the same paired framing, but flagged as a guardrail, not the main answer.\\n\\n## Consequential assumptions and uncertainties\\n\\n### Assumptions (must hold for the design to be valid)\\n- **A1. Hardware.** A single high-end GPU class (NVIDIA A100 80GB or H100), CUDA 12.x, with enough VRAM for the largest cell (13B in W4A4 with KV-cache FP16 plus activations buffer).\\n- **A2. Faithful QuaRot recipe.** Rotation matrix construction, per-channel/head clipping search, GPTQ-style weight quantization on rotated weights, and the small set of outlier channels kept in higher precision are reproduced as in the paper. Any deviation shifts the result.\\n- **A3. LLaMa-2 weights.** Access to the official Meta-released checkpoints under their license.\\n- **A4. KV-cache stays FP16** by default in QuaRot (its published default), so W4A4 does not silently include KV quantization.\\n- **A5. Identical kernel stack across conditions** (FlashAttention-2 or SDPA), so the comparison reflects quantization and not kernel choice.\\n- **A6. Calibration data** is WikiText-2 train, fixed sequence count, and not reused for evaluation.\\n- **A7. This design is the deliverable**; the bubblewrap is not expected to execute it.\\n\\n### Uncertainties (open items I would resolve before the final design)\\n- **U1. KV-cache quantization.** QuaRot reports an experimental 4-bit KV cache. Should +KV4 be a fourth cell, or out of scope? My default is \\\"out of scope, mentioned as extension,\\\" but I want confirmation.\\n- **U2. \\\"End-to-end W4A4\\\" perimeter.** Whether to count the residual outlier channels as still end-to-end 4-bit. Proposed alignment: report exactly what the paper calls W4A4 and document the small FP16 outlier percentage as a qualifier.\\n- **U3. Canonical decoding metric.** TPOT (steady-state, single-token) vs aggregate tokens/s. Proposed default: report both, with TPOT primary for the decoding impact claim.\\n- **U4. 70B scope.** If compute is tight, drop 70B rather than running a degraded 7B-style protocol on it.\\n- **U5. Environment gap.** The actual measurement will not occur in this bubblewrap; I can produce only the design document here.\\n- **U6. Eval subset size.** LM-Eval-Harness subsets chosen here are small for runtime control; the researcher may want a different breadth.\\n\\n### Hypothesized direction and magnitude (labeled as hypothesis, not measured)\\n- **H1. Prefill under W4A4.** Small or neutral effect at short prompts (kernel-launch and quantization overhead can wipe out bandwidth savings) and a modest positive effect at long prompts because activation bandwidth drops. Order-of-magnitude guess: 0–15% relative TTFT change at 7B for prompts ≥ 2k tokens; 13B likely benefits slightly more due to higher memory pressure.\\n- **H2. Decoding under W4A4.** Clearly positive on memory-bound regimes (high context, large batch); aggregate throughput tokens/s plausibly ~1.5×–3× FP16; TPOT reduction in the same ballpark.\\n- **H3. W4A16 reference.** Smaller version of H2; small but positive decoding effect, near-neutral prefill.\\n- **H4. Quality.** Δ perplexity likely sub-1-point; small LM-Eval subset will be noisy and may sit inside that noise.\\n\\n### What counts as a \\\"meaningful\\\" prefill vs decoding impact threshold (proposed, to confirm)\\n- **T1. Prefill:** |Δ TTFT| ≥ 5% (5% slowdown or 5% speedup) relative to FP16 is meaningful; below that is kernel/noise floor.\\n- **T2. Decode:** |Δ TPOT| ≥ 10% is meaningful overall, with a tighter ≥ 5% threshold in clearly memory-bound cells (long context, batch ≥ 4).\\n- **T3. Memory:** ≥ 2× peak-memory reduction vs FP16 is the meaningful bar for the W4A4 claim.\\n\\n### Decisions awaiting researcher input before I finalize the design\\n1. Confirm or change **KV-cache quantization** policy (U1).\\n2. Confirm 70B is or isn't in scope (U4).\\n3. Confirm the **impact thresholds** T1/T2/T3, or supply alternatives.\\n4. Confirm that an **intermediate W4A16 cell** is wanted as a reference, since it costs another column of measurements.\\n5. Confirm the **LM-Eval subset** identity, or whether perplexity alone is enough as the quality guardrail.\",\"evidence\":\"Inspection results from this turn:\\n\\n- `ls -la /workspace` shows a single file `task.json` (405 bytes) owned by uid 1776737281; directory has no other subdirectories.\\n- `find /workspace -maxdepth 3 -type f` returns only `/workspace/task.json`; `find /workspace -maxdepth 3 -type d` returns only `/workspace`.\\n- `cat /workspace/task.json` confirms the public task question, the `documents.track.md` note \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\\\", and that `datasets` is empty.\\n- `python3 --version` reports 3.12.3; `nproc` reports 24; `free -h` reports ~125 GiB total RAM; `which nvidia-smi` indicates nvidia-smi is absent on PATH (which itself is also absent), and no `nvidia*` device lines are present, consistent with the task descriptor's `gpu_enabled: false`.\\n- Uname: `Linux d33eaef-lcedt 7.0.0-38-generic ... x86_64`, matching a sandbox bubblewrap.\\n\\nReproduction commands:\\n  ls -la /workspace\\n  find /workspace -maxdepth 3\\n  cat /workspace/task.json\\n  python3 --version && nproc && free -h\",\"assumptions\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":\"Hypothesized effect directions/magnitudes (H1–H4) are guesses from prior published characterizations, not measurements under this task.</item>\",\"$text\":\"Experimental design faithfully follows the QuaRot methodology as published; deviations would shift results and must be documented if they occur.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Design only; no execution in this bubblewrap (consistent with task.json's `documents.track.md` note and the explicit no-network/no-deps/no-GPU environment).</item>\\n\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"Concrete hardware and CUDA stack available at execution time, which currently are not specified beyond \\\"GPU enabled if supplied.\\\"</item>\",\"$text\":\"Identity / size of the LM-Eval-Harness quality subset (U6).</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Whether the W4A16 intermediate cell is desired — it costs another column of measurements but cleanly attributes the W4A4 effect to weight vs activation quantization.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Whether the proposed meaningful-impact thresholds (5% TTFT, 10% TPOT with 5% in memory-bound cells, 2× memory) are acceptable, or whether the researcher wants stricter/looser bars.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Whether LLaMa-2 70B is in scope given single-GPU assumption and the unspecified hardware budget (U4).</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Whether to include an additional +KV4 cell covering QuaRot's experimental 4-bit KV cache (U1).</item>\\n\"}]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-b770aea1-aa56-45f5-a84c-187b19aa1ef4", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 16}
